  <text>
    <body>
      <p>Engineers, ironfounders, millwrights and brassfounders worked in the project area from the late 1850s. In the nineteenth century the largest were the foundries: the <ref target="civic?id=Carlton%20Foundry">Carlton Foundry</ref> in <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref>, the <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Foundry">Victoria Foundry</ref> in <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Jenning%27s%20Foundry">Jenning's Foundry</ref> in <ref target="civic?id=Berkley%20Street">Berkley Street</ref>, and later the <ref target="civic?id=Atlas%20Co.%20of%20Engineers">Atlas Co. of Engineers</ref> in <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>. <ref target="civic?id=Robert%20Bodington">Robert Bodington</ref>, millwright and later milling engineer, is listed in <ref target="civic?id=Queensberry%20Street">Queensberry Street</ref> for eighty years, from 1860 to 1940, and the <ref target="civic?id=Nicholson%20implement%20makers">Nicholson implement makers</ref> made agricultural implements in <ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> from 1859. In the twentieth century the directories list electrical, textile and fire protection engineers, and from the 1920s many motor engineers.</p>
      <p>The lists below are drawn only from the directories. Named works link to their own entries, and most of those haven't been written yet. Firms and engineers listed under their own names are given as the directories print them. <ref target="civic?id=Engineering">Engineering Firms</ref> and <ref target="civic?id=The%20Engineers%20of%20University%20Square">The Engineers of University Square</ref> say more about some of them.</p>
