          <row><cell><ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Foundry">Victoria Foundry</ref></cell><cell><ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref></cell><cell>7; 188–206 (1890), 188 (1900)</cell><cell>1873–1900</cell><cell>Phillips &amp; McWalter (1873), then Phillips, McWalter &amp; Chambers (1874–1890), then McWalter &amp; Mangels (1900). Niven, Phillips and McWalter's foundry was at No. 7 in 1870–1872 (<ref target="civic?id=Phillips%20Niven">Phillips Niven</ref>); it isn't known whether this was the same business. John Payne &amp; Sons, ironfounders, were at 188–208 Victoria Street from 1900 to 1920.</cell></row>
