      <div>
        <head>Motor engineers</head>
        <p>Motor engineers appear from 1925 and are listed here by street, with numbers and years.</p>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Bouverie%20Street">Bouverie Street</ref>: H. H. Schmidt (65–67, 1925–1930), Jas. O. Davies (163, 1930) and Baker &amp; Shaw (163, 1940).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Berkley%20Street">Berkley Street</ref>: Dunlop &amp; Wilson (25–27, 1925), then F. W. Davey &amp; Co. (25–27, 1935–1940), and L. Bloom (122–128, 1940).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Sydney%20Road">Sydney Road</ref>: N. V. Bodinnar (12, 1925).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Pelham%20Street">Pelham Street</ref>: National Motor Reconditioning Pty Ltd (156, 1930–1935).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Queensberry%20Street">Queensberry Street</ref>: Replacement Parts Pty Ltd (264–270, 1930), Lea-Wright Motors Pty Ltd (181–187, 1935) and Marshall &amp; Brede (183–185, 1940).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Barkly%20Place">Barkly Place</ref>: J. Turner (16, 1935).</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Swanston%20Street">Swanston Street</ref>: Coxhill &amp; Hewitt (520–524), Perrier &amp; Hankin (636–640) and Latrobe Motors Pty Ltd (642–644), all 1935.</item>
          <item><ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref>: Bussing Diesel Vehicles Pty Ltd (6, 1940).</item>
        </list>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Notes</head>
        <list rend="bulleted">
          <item>The Victoria Foundry and Niven, Phillips and McWalter's foundry are both listed at No. 7 <ref target="civic?id=Victoria%20Street">Victoria Street</ref>, but under different names, so they are kept apart. In 1900 the Victoria Foundry (No. 188) and John Payne &amp; Sons (No. 208) are listed in the same year.</item>
          <item>Joseph Royal is also listed as a wheelwright and blacksmith in <ref target="civic?id=Leicester%20Street">Leicester Street</ref> (see <ref target="civic?id=Blacksmiths">Blacksmiths</ref>).</item>
          <item>University engineering staff and the engineering school in the University grounds are left out (see <ref target="civic?id=Schools">Schools</ref>).</item>
        </list>
      </div>
      <div>
        <head>Sources</head>
        <p>Every listing can be browsed in <ref target="search?q=engineer&amp;src=directories">search</ref>. The directories are yearly to 1880 and then every five years, so years are the first and last directories that list each entry.</p>
